    "body": "**TLDR:** On main, a Qwen3.5 generator with CUDA graphs fails to start: vLLM's profile and capture runs compile the `offset_rmsnorm` region 9 times, past Dynamo's limit of 8. This PR raises the region's limit to 16, as `fused_binary_activation` already does.\n\n**Problem**\n1. The region compiles `OffsetRMSNorm.forward(self, x)`, so Dynamo recompiles when the rank or strides of `x`, or the class of `self`, change.\n2. Qwen3.5 passes 3 layouts of `x`: rank-2 (block norms), rank-3 and strided rank-3 (q/k norms).\n3. With FSDP on the generator, the final norm becomes an `FSDPOffsetRMSNorm`, a 4th case.\n4. Each case compiles up to 3 versions (graphs): the first token count, then the token count as dynamic, then a single token (Dynamo specializes sizes 0 and 1).\n5. Here that is 9 graphs, one past the limit.\n\n**Solution**\n1. `recompile_limit=16` on the region.\n2. The count doesn't grow with the number of CUDA graph sizes: vLLM captured 19 sizes here and the region still compiled 9 graphs. Only a new layout or class adds graphs, up to 3 each, so 16 fits 5 cases.\n\n**Results**\n```text\nQwen3.5-9B generator, TP1, FULL CUDA graphs, 1x H100, torch 2.15.0.dev20261005\nmain:     [0/8] torch._dynamo hit config.recompile_limit (8), engine fails to start\nthis PR:  OffsetRMSNorm.forward compiles 9 graphs, engine starts\n```\n\nYou may ask: why not compile a free function `(x, weight, eps)`? It would drop the class case but leave 7 of 8 graphs, one layout away from crashing again.\n\n**Test plan**\n- The engine above (a local script with `TORCH_LOGS=recompiles`), on an earlier main.\n- On this main, with the weight-sync memory fix (separate PR) also applied: Qwen3.5-9B and Qwen3.5-35B-A3B generators at TP1 start with FULL CUDA graphs and pass two weight syncs.\n- A 2-GPU Qwen3.5-4B-Base RL run for 8 steps, also with the weight-sync fix, on an earlier main.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
